# enterprise-home-lab
# Project 01 — Three-Node Proxmox VE Deployment

My goal for this part of the project is to install Proxmox VE 9.2 on all three of my Dell Optiplex 7050. Please refer to the Project 00 README file to see my thought process behind my homelab !!

## Objective
Deploy a three-node virtualization environment to support hands-on training in Linux system administration, networking, cybersecurity, and infrastructure automation.

## Hardware
- 3 × Dell OptiPlex 7050 Micro
- Intel Core i7 processors
- 16 GB RAM per node
- 512 GB M.2 SSD per node
- GeekPi Rackmate T1

## Technology
- Proxmox Virtual Environment
- Debian Linux
- Linux bridges
- TCP/IP networking
- SSH

## Implementation
1. Created a bootable Proxmox installation USB.
2. Configured BIOS virtualization and storage settings.
3. Installed Proxmox VE on all three physical servers.
4. Configured management networking.
5. Verified that all three nodes were accessible from a separate computer.

## Validation Commands

```bash
hostnamectl
ip -br addr
ip route
pveversion -v
```

## Results
Successfully installed Proxmox VE on three physical hosts and verified remote access to their management interfaces.

